[[:db/retract 17592186179973 :question/answer-fields 17592186177507] {:db/id 17592186179967 :question/problem "![](images/11/11c759098d959c7dbdcb81686640bfc6a01d4dc0f9b12e6ff45f3028ddc4d2db.png)\n\nThe gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be a contour plot of $f(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\nObserve that the given field vectors are perpendicular to the level curves in the following picture.\n\n![](images/4b/4b20823340d89e0ff4aa2fd65078d3819e8b218419a54ea632c1109e698858ab.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](images/14/14c453b9fcf4670a2356b730253dd7f411b989abde303f059ebb5a9d559a4eff.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177471 :answer-field/correct 17592186177472 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d9aa2a3-1ea1-5a5e-9577-ca5789b6206d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d9aa2a3-1ea1-5a5e-9577-ca5789b6206d" :question/id #uuid "6d9aa2a3-1ea1-5a5e-9577-ca5789b6206d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122737" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =2(x-y)\\,i-2(x-y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(2,1),$ $(1,2),$ and $(1,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1) & =2\\cdot (2-1)\\,i-2\\cdot (2-1)\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,2) & =2\\cdot (1-2)\\,i-2\\cdot (1-2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,i-2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,j=4\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9f1a53d-9e00-54ab-b914-f5c8b1d4efa0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9f1a53d-9e00-54ab-b914-f5c8b1d4efa0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9f1a53d-9e00-54ab-b914-f5c8b1d4efa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5dba748-9027-5a4a-bf33-0feb67920158" "answer-cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" "answer-0afc3cbd-80cd-5f79-95d1-b02b58d14af7" "answer-25ed12c7-2e43-5b16-b2e3-173b3c5367b8" "answer-99f6e268-33a9-5e9a-a609-e6ee2c4c38d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5dba748-9027-5a4a-bf33-0feb67920158" :answer/id #uuid "c5dba748-9027-5a4a-bf33-0feb67920158" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4c/4c5c4b297d1aaaa672628f0621e8ed71fbacedd9f418d7d7068da8cba5847315.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" :answer/id #uuid "cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0afc3cbd-80cd-5f79-95d1-b02b58d14af7" :answer/id #uuid "0afc3cbd-80cd-5f79-95d1-b02b58d14af7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ce/ce7690cdb4a4da4841dc7f551b73d379945141964de4f9de00dbe6a39a6e36e8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25ed12